data.content:
Here's the `SortableList` component:

**Key design points:**

- **Generic** (`@typeparam TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Immutable input** — `Items` parameter is copied into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet`, so the parent's collection is never mutated.
- **`OnOrderChanged`** fires after every move, passing a read-only copy of the reordered list.
- **`@key`** on each `<li>` for efficient diffing.
- **Buttons disable** at boundaries (can't move first item up or last item down).

**Usage matches your example:**

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
